# Build context for services/<svc>/Dockerfile is the repository root (P0-07a).
# Keep out: VCS, caches, secrets, JS, design, docs, tests, infra. Keep in (do NOT list here): pyproject.toml,
# uv.lock, packages, services, config, contracts, prompts, templates (the uv workspace install needs them).
.git
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
node_modules
**/node_modules
.env*
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
# Credential files at any depth (OAuth client secrets, saved tokens, key files): a bare pattern only matches the
# context root, so every one of these is a `**/` pattern.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/client_secret*.json
**/token*.json
**/credentials.json
**/service-account*.json
**/*-credentials.json
**/application_default_credentials.json
design
!design/tokens.json
docs
infra
apps
meet-bot
scratch*
*.log
**/tests
packages/contracts-ts
# Services read the schemas, the event registry and the generated models under contracts/, never its test fixtures
# or rule notes (the sample world ships as package data in tilo_api/sample_data).
contracts/fixtures
contracts/**/*.md
evals/*
!evals/pyproject.toml
